<item>
            <title>[KYLIN-5454] Downloading the async query result may cause OOM error</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-5454</link>
                <project id="12316121" key="KYLIN">Kylin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When using &lt;tt&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://host:port/kylin/api/async_query/&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://host:port/kylin/api/async_query/\&lt;/a&gt;{query_id}/result_download?&lt;/tt&gt; to get asynchronous query result, out-of-memory error might occur. The reason is the formatting process while downloading the result needs read &amp;amp; write, and there is batch processing rather than streaming processing. Therefore, a refactor is needed for async query. The main idea of revision is to move the formatting from downloading result from HDFS to processing &amp;amp; saving query result on HDFS, and use streaming read &amp;amp; write instead.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The details of design are in the attached file.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
